# Anti-Slop Design Standards

> "Slop" = generic, template-looking, lifeless UI. This project has ZERO tolerance for slop.
> Every screen must look like it was designed by a studio that charges $300/hr.

## The Slop Test — If ANY of these are true, the code FAILS review:
1. ❌ Using default browser fonts (Times New Roman, serif, system default sans-serif without explicit stack)
2. ❌ Using pure `#000000` black on pure `#FFFFFF` white backgrounds
3. ❌ Generic blue (`#007bff`, `#0066cc`) as primary color
4. ❌ Uniform padding/margin everywhere (everything is `p-4`, `m-4`)
5. ❌ All text the same size or weight
6. ❌ Buttons that look like Bootstrap defaults
7. ❌ Cards with identical shadows and border-radius without hierarchy
8. ❌ Empty space that serves no compositional purpose
9. ❌ Icons used as decoration with no functional meaning
10. ❌ Color palette with more than 2 competing saturated hues (unless intentionally designed)

## Typography Rules

### Font Stack
- Use a curated sans-serif: **Inter**, **Geist**, **Satoshi**, or **Outfit** via Google Fonts or `next/font`.
- Monospace for code/data: **JetBrains Mono**, **Geist Mono**, or **Fira Code**.
- Load with `next/font/google` or `next/font/local` for zero-CLS font loading.

### Type Scale (MANDATORY)
Establish and reuse a consistent type scale. Example using Tailwind:
```
Hero/Display:  text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl  font-bold    tracking-tight
Page title:    text-2xl md:text-3xl               font-semibold tracking-tight
Section head:  text-xl md:text-2xl                font-semibold
Card title:    text-lg                            font-medium
Body:          text-base                          font-normal   leading-relaxed
Caption/meta:  text-sm                            font-normal   text-muted-foreground
Micro/label:   text-xs                            font-medium   uppercase tracking-wider
```

### Rules
- **Headings MUST use `tracking-tight`** (letter-spacing: -0.025em). Loose headings look amateur.
- **Body text MUST use `leading-relaxed`** (line-height: 1.625) or `leading-7`. Cramped text is unreadable.
- **Contrast between heading weight and body weight** must be ≥2 steps (e.g., bold headings, normal body).
- **Never use more than 3 font weights** on a single screen.

## Color System

### Dark Mode (PRIMARY — This app is dark-mode-first)
```css
/* Semantic tokens — NOT raw hex values scattered in components */
--background:       hsl(0 0% 3.9%);      /* Near-black, NOT pure black */
--foreground:        hsl(0 0% 98%);       /* Near-white, NOT pure white */
--muted:             hsl(0 0% 14.9%);     /* Subtle backgrounds */
--muted-foreground:  hsl(0 0% 63.9%);     /* Secondary text */
--card:              hsl(0 0% 6%);        /* Card surfaces */
--card-foreground:   hsl(0 0% 98%);
--border:            hsl(0 0% 14.9%);     /* Subtle borders */
--ring:              hsl(0 0% 83.1%);     /* Focus rings */
--primary:           /* YOUR brand hue */ ;
--primary-foreground:/* Contrast color for text on primary */;
--destructive:       hsl(0 62.8% 50.6%);
--accent:            hsl(0 0% 14.9%);
--accent-foreground: hsl(0 0% 98%);
```

### Rules
- **NEVER hardcode hex/rgb values in components**. Use CSS custom properties or Tailwind semantic tokens.
- **Surfaces must have hierarchy**: background → card → elevated card. Minimum 3 elevation levels.
- **Borders should be subtle** (`border-white/10` or `border-[hsl(0,0%,15%)]`), not harsh.
- **Text hierarchy through opacity/color, not just size**: primary text (`opacity-100`), secondary (`opacity-70`), muted (`opacity-40`).
- **Accent colors must be used sparingly** — max 10-15% of the visible surface area.

## Spacing & Layout

### The 4px Grid
All spacing must be multiples of 4px: `4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64, 80, 96`.
- Component internal padding: `12–16px`
- Between related items: `8–12px`
- Between sections: `32–48px`
- Page margins: `16–24px` mobile, `32–64px` desktop

### Rules
- **Generous whitespace > cramped layouts**. When in doubt, add more space.
- **Group related elements tightly**, separate unrelated elements generously. This creates visual hierarchy through proximity (Gestalt principle).
- **Never center-align body text** over 2 lines. Left-align for readability.
- **Max content width**: `max-w-2xl` for text, `max-w-6xl` for dashboards. Never full-width text.

## Component Quality Standards

### Buttons
- Must have **4 states minimum**: default, hover, active (pressed), disabled.
- Primary buttons: filled with primary color, slight shadow.
- Secondary buttons: ghost/outline style, subtle background on hover.
- **Active state**: `scale(0.97–0.98)` transform. MANDATORY.
- **Disabled state**: `opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed`. Never just gray out the text.
- **Icon + label buttons**: Icon must be `16–20px`, with `8px` gap to label.

### Cards
- Must have **differentiated elevation levels**: flat, raised, floating.
- Hover state: subtle lift + shadow increase OR border glow.
- **Content inside cards** must have consistent internal padding.
- **Never stack cards without visual separation** (gap, dividers, or background contrast).

### Forms & Inputs
- Inputs must have: placeholder (muted), focus ring (primary color), error state (destructive + message), disabled state.
- Labels above inputs, not as placeholders that disappear.
- Error messages appear with a slide-down animation, not instant.

### Empty States
- **NEVER** show a blank page with just "No data" text.
- Use an illustration or icon (≥48px), a message, and a CTA button if applicable.
- Empty states should feel intentional, not broken.

## Dark Mode Polish Checklist
- [ ] No pure `#000` backgrounds — use `hsl(0 0% 3.9%)` or similar near-black
- [ ] No pure `#FFF` text — use `hsl(0 0% 98%)` or `text-zinc-50`
- [ ] Images/illustrations have appropriate dark mode variants or overlays
- [ ] Shadows use `rgba(0,0,0,0.3–0.5)` not `rgba(0,0,0,0.1)` (too invisible on dark)
- [ ] Borders are visible but subtle (`white/10` or `zinc-800`)
- [ ] Charts/graphs use colors that work on dark backgrounds (check contrast)
- [ ] No "washed out" or "foggy" sections — every element has clear contrast
- [ ] Status colors (success, warning, error) are adjusted for dark mode readability

## The Final Test
Look at your screen from 2 meters away. Can you identify:
1. The most important element? (visual hierarchy)
2. Where to take action? (CTA prominence)
3. How content is grouped? (spatial relationships)

If not, the design FAILS and needs revision.
